{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q3604536","formula":"H₂O₃Si","hill":"H2O3Si","elements":["H","O","Si"],"composition":{"H":2.0,"O":3.0,"Si":1.0},"names":{"en":"Metasilicic acid","uk":"Метасилікатна кислота"},"descriptions":{"en":"Metasilicic acid is a hypothetical chemical compound with formula (HO)2SiO. The free acid slowly polymerises in aqueous solution even at low concentrations and cannot be isolated under normal conditions. Compounds including the conjugate base are known as metasilicates and occur widely in nature as inosilicates.","uk":"Метасиліка́тна (метакремнієва) кислота́ H2SiO3 — дуже слабка, двохоснóвна кислота. Нерозчинна у воді. Вона не діє на індикатори, не реагує з металами, багатьма оснóвними оксидами, нерозчинними основами, солями, але взаємодіє з лугами і розкладається при нагріванні."},"fame":9,"pubchemCid":14768,"mass":78.099,"charge":0,"smiles":"O[Si](=O)O","inchikey":"IJKVHSBPTUYDLN-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"dihydroxy(oxo)silane","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"14768","atoms":6,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":0.0,"y":0.057,"z":0.361,"el":"Si"},{"x":1.37,"y":-0.752,"z":-0.114,"el":"O"},{"x":-1.371,"y":-0.751,"z":-0.114,"el":"O"},{"x":0.001,"y":1.446,"z":-0.133,"el":"O"},{"x":2.232,"y":-0.382,"z":0.139,"el":"H"},{"x":-1.524,"y":-0.873,"z":-1.066,"el":"H"}],"bonds":[[0,1,1],[0,2,1],[0,3,2],[1,4,1],[2,5,1]]},"sources":[{"role":"identity","name":"Wikidata","url":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q3604536","license":"CC0 1.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (en)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Metasilicic_acid","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (uk)","url":"https://uk.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D0%9C%D0%B5%D1%82%D0%B0%D1%81%D0%B8%D0%BB%D1%96%D0%BA%D0%B0%D1%82%D0%BD%D0%B0_%D0%BA%D0%B8%D1%81%D0%BB%D0%BE